<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>55.0</apiVersion>
    <description>When a new user is added, a contact record is created as well</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Create Contact from User {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>User: Create Contact from User</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>OriginBuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <actionCalls>
        <description>C1: fired from Create_Contact&apos;s faultConnector when the Contact record create throws (e.g. a validation rule). Handling the fault here means the transaction that created the User does not roll back.</description>
        <name>Notify_Admins_Fault</name>
        <label>Notify Admins - Contact Create Failed</label>
        <locationX>708</locationX>
        <locationY>674</locationY>
        <actionName>emailSimple</actionName>
        <actionType>emailSimple</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailAddresses</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>AdminEmailAddresses</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailBody</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>tpl_FaultBody</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailSubject</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Salesforce: Contact creation failed for new user</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>sendRichBody</name>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>emailSimple</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <actionCalls>
        <description>C2: fired when $Record.FirstName is blank. The Contact create is skipped rather than pushing malformed data past FIist_Name_Cannot_be_Blank, and an admin is told so the source directory object can be fixed.</description>
        <name>Notify_Admins_Skipped_Blank_Name</name>
        <label>Notify Admins - Contact Not Created, Blank First Name</label>
        <locationX>972</locationX>
        <locationY>350</locationY>
        <actionName>emailSimple</actionName>
        <actionType>emailSimple</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailAddresses</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>AdminEmailAddresses</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailBody</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>tpl_SkippedBlankNameBody</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailSubject</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Salesforce: Contact NOT created - blank first name, action needed</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>sendRichBody</name>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>emailSimple</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <actionCalls>
        <description>C3: fired when a Contact already exists with this User&apos;s email. The create is skipped so re-provisioning does not produce a second Contact on the LBR account.</description>
        <name>Notify_Admins_Skipped_Duplicate</name>
        <label>Notify Admins - Contact Not Created, Duplicate Found</label>
        <locationX>1236</locationX>
        <locationY>350</locationY>
        <actionName>emailSimple</actionName>
        <actionType>emailSimple</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailAddresses</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>AdminEmailAddresses</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailBody</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>tpl_SkippedDuplicateBody</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailSubject</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Salesforce: Contact creation skipped - duplicate email found</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>sendRichBody</name>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>emailSimple</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <decisions>
        <description>C2/C3 guard. Split into two distinct outcomes (rather than one combined rule) so a blank-name skip and a duplicate skip produce distinguishable notifications - one needs IT to fix the directory, the other is benign.</description>
        <name>Check_Contact_Prerequisites</name>
        <label>Check Contact Prerequisites</label>
        <locationX>440</locationX>
        <locationY>350</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Create_Contact</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Safe to Create</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Blank_First_Name</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.FirstName</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Notify_Admins_Skipped_Blank_Name</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Blank First Name</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>Duplicate_Contact_Exists</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Existing_Contact</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Notify_Admins_Skipped_Duplicate</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Duplicate Contact Exists</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_Contact</name>
        <label>Create Contact</label>
        <locationX>440</locationX>
        <locationY>458</locationY>
        <faultConnector>
            <targetReference>Notify_Admins_Fault</targetReference>
        </faultConnector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AccountId</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>0016g00001AQ7lXAAT</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Department</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Department</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Email</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Email</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>FirstName</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.FirstName</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>LastName</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.LastName</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Phone</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Phone</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>ReportsToId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.ManagerId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>Contact</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordLookups>
        <description>Sources the admin recipient list from the existing Flow_Error_Email__mdt CMDT record (the same custom metadata the org&apos;s Debug_Flow_Error_Handling template pattern uses) rather than hardcoding an address or a Group Id in this flow&apos;s metadata.</description>
        <name>Get_Admin_Email_Recipients</name>
        <label>Get Admin Email Recipients</label>
        <locationX>440</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Existing_Contact</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>DeveloperName</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Error_Email_List</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Flow_Error_Email__mdt</object>
        <outputAssignments>
            <assignToReference>AdminEmailAddresses</assignToReference>
            <field>Comma_Separated_Email_List__c</field>
        </outputAssignments>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <description>C3: duplicate guard. Looks up an existing Contact by the User&apos;s email before create so re-provisioning does not risk a second Contact on the LBR account.</description>
        <name>Get_Existing_Contact</name>
        <label>Get Existing Contact by Email</label>
        <locationX>440</locationX>
        <locationY>242</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Check_Contact_Prerequisites</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Email</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Email</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Contact</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Admin_Email_Recipients</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <object>User</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Create</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
    <textTemplates>
        <description>C1: fault notification body. Includes $Flow.FaultMessage - without it the notification is useless per the runbook.</description>
        <name>tpl_FaultBody</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>true</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>Contact creation failed for a newly provisioned User. The User record was created successfully; the Contact was not.

User Id: {!$Record.Id}
Username: {!$Record.Username}
Email: {!$Record.Email}
First Name: {!$Record.FirstName}
Last Name: {!$Record.LastName}

Fault message:
{!$Flow.FaultMessage}</text>
    </textTemplates>
    <textTemplates>
        <description>C2: blank first name skip notification body.</description>
        <name>tpl_SkippedBlankNameBody</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>true</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>A new User was provisioned with a blank first name, so no matching Contact was created (this is expected behaviour - see Create_Contact_from_User v4).

User Id: {!$Record.Id}
Username: {!$Record.Username}
Email: {!$Record.Email}
First Name: {!$Record.FirstName}
Last Name: {!$Record.LastName}

Action needed: populate the first name on the source directory object and re-sync so the Contact can be created.</text>
    </textTemplates>
    <textTemplates>
        <description>C3: duplicate email skip notification body.</description>
        <name>tpl_SkippedDuplicateBody</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>true</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>A new User was provisioned, but a Contact already exists with a matching email address, so no new Contact was created (this is expected behaviour - see Create_Contact_from_User v4).

User Id: {!$Record.Id}
Username: {!$Record.Username}
Email: {!$Record.Email}
First Name: {!$Record.FirstName}
Last Name: {!$Record.LastName}
Existing Contact Id: {!Get_Existing_Contact.Id}

No action needed unless the existing Contact is incorrect.</text>
    </textTemplates>
    <variables>
        <name>AdminEmailAddresses</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <isCollection>false</isCollection>
        <isInput>false</isInput>
        <isOutput>false</isOutput>
    </variables>
    <variables>
        <name>var_flowname</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <isCollection>false</isCollection>
        <isInput>true</isInput>
        <isOutput>true</isOutput>
        <value>
            <stringValue>User: Create Contact from User</stringValue>
        </value>
    </variables>
</Flow>
